MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
GS-9: Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-8 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
1) Conduct screenings to identify family violence dynamics, safety assessment and crisis intervention techniques;
2) Develop, implement and deliver training, parenting education and coaching to military and civilian families;
3) Provide information and referral to military organizations, missions, lifestyles, and associated stressors that can impact family development and unity during childbearing years; and
4) Market and promote programs and services through a variety of military and civilian stakeholder's venues to provide appropriate preventive intervention to families. NOTE: This information must be supported in your resume to be considered for the position. GS-8: Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-7 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
1) Conduct screenings and assessments to determine if support services are warranted;
2) Develop and sustain partnerships with military and civilian family/health service providers;
3) Provide parenting education training and coaching to deter unhealthy parenting attitudes and beliefs; and
4) Maintain case files to compile statistics, document work and other program data. NOTE: This information must be supported in your resume to be considered for the position. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/0100/social-services-series-0187/ Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
